                <pb facs="0985" n="1943" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1943"/>

                <head>No. 68.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31, 1887</date>.
                        (Received September 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your circular, dated July 9,
                    1887, suggesting the abolition of tonnage duties and equivalent charges on
                    navigation, I have to report that the same was forwarded to Mr. Mariscal, and he
                    has replied that he has sent the circular to the treasury department, requesting
                    information on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. C. Manning.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
